1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT =Fredrika Eleonora von Düben=
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Von_D%C3%BCben_nr_139#TAB_2 '''Fredrika Eleonora von Düben'''], född 1738-12-17. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Hovfröken hos''' drottningen 1757. Överhovmästarinna hos änkedrottning Lovisa Ulrika. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Död 1808-01-03''' i Linköping. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Gift 1759-04-09''' i Stockholm med riksrådet och överstemarskalken, greve Nils Adam [https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Bielke_nr_29 Bielke], i hans 2:a gifte, född 1724, död 1792.
2 CONT
2 CONT /////
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fredrika_Eleonora_von_D%C3%BCben '''Fredrika Eleonora von Düben'''] was a Swedish dilettante painter and embroidery artist.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Fredrika Eleonora''' was born to '''Baron Joachim von Düben''' and '''Catharina Eleonora Temming'''. Her father was a nephew of royal favourite [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emerentia_von_D%C3%BCben Emerentia von Düben] and se
2 CONC rved as the cabinet secretary of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ulrika_Eleonora,_Queen_of_Sweden Ulrika Eleonora], Queen of Sweden.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In 1759, she married''' '''Count Nils Adam Bielke''' who was previously been married to her relative [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ulrika_Eleonora_von_D%C3%BCben Ulrika Eleonora von Düben]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''She was an''' honorary member of the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Royal_Swedish_Academy_of_Fine_Arts Royal Swedish Academy of Arts] after having participated in the art exhibition with an embroidered landscape in white silk. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''She was maid''' of honor to Queen [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louisa_Ulrika_of_Prussia Louisa Ulrika of Prussia] from 1757-59 and Chief Court mistress, Mistress of the Robes of the Swedish queen dowager in 1771-1782
2 CONT <br/>
2 CONT <br/>
