1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://fi.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kustaa_Horn
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gustav_Horn,_Count_of_Pori
2 CONT
2 CONT Count '''Gustav Horn af Björneborg''' (October 22, 1592 – May 10, 1657) was a Swedish/Finnish soldier and politician. He was the youngest son of Field Marshal Carl Horn and Agneta von Dellwig, born while his father was imprisoned 
2 CONC in Örbyhus Castle, after the defeat against Russians.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born of the Finnish noble family Horn of Kankas, and was appointed member of the Royal Council in 1625, Field Marshal in 1628, Governor General of Livonia in 1652 and Lord High Constable since 1653. In the Thirty Years' War
2 CONC  (1618–1648), he was instrumental as a commander in securing victory at the Battle of Breitenfeld, in 1631. He was High Councillor of the realm in 1625, elevated to rank of field marshal in 1628, and sometimes commander-in-chief o
2 CONC f Swedish forces in Germany during Thirty Years' War. After the war, he served as Governor-General of Livonia 1652, President of War department and Lord High Constable in 1653. In 1651, Queen Christina created him Count of Pori.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gustaf Horn  af Björneborg. s.22.10.1592 k.10.5.1657. Suomalainen marsalkka ,valtaneuvos 1624, Porin kreivi 1651, Liivinmaan kenraalikuvernööri 1652 ja valtakunnan marsalkka 1653. Kolmikymmenvuotisessa sodassa hän oli Kustaa II Aa
2 CONC dolfin lähin mies.  Hän oli Evert Hornin poika. Sai kuningatar Kristiinalta Porin kreivikunnan johon kuului Porin kaupunki ja yli 350 taloa Ulvilassa ,Huittisissa ja Kokemäellä. Kreivikunta purettiin reduktiossa 1681 –pso Christin
2 CONC a Oxenstierna af Eka och Lindö
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fi.wikipedia.org/wiki/Breitenfeldin_ensimm%C3%A4inen_taistelu
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Breitenfeld_(1631)
