1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/De_Geer_af_Leufsta_nr_131#TAB_11 '''''Carl'' Fredrik De Geer af Leufsta'''], head of the family and owner of the fideikommissarie after his cousin Lois 1925-11-30. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Born 1860-11-24''' in Geneva. Licenciées-lettres 1879. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Volunteer in the''' Swedish Life Guards (Svea livgarde )1880. Student at the War College 1880. Graduated 1881. Re-admitted 1881. Graduated 1882. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Second lieutenant''' in the Svea livgarde 1882. Retired 1887. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Swedish-Norwegian''' Consul General in Geneva 1888. Joined the Svea livgarde reserve 1889. RVO 1899. RNO 1907. Resigned as Consul General 1920. KVO2kl 1920. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Has published''' several works of fiction in French language. Owns Malagnov near Geneva. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Died 1947-04-04''' in Geneva (Hammarby förs., Stockholm, db nr 9). 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Married 1887-03-11''' in Eaux-Vives in Switzerland to '''Anne Suzanne-''Henriette'' Krieg''', born 1866-04-14 in Eaux-Vives, daughter of Alexandre-Adrien Krieg and Elisabet Dufour, died 1931-12-04 in Genève, (Protestant parish 
2 CONC in Eaux.Vives).
