1 NAME Charles Peter /Layard/ BA
2 GIVN Charles Peter
2 SURN Layard
2 NSFX BA
2 _MARNM Layard
1 NAME Rev. Charles Peter Layard
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE BET 19 FEB 1748 AND 19 FEB 1749
1 DEAT
2 DATE 11 APR 1803
1 TITL Reverend
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Charles Peter Layard, F.R.S., D.D. was Dean of Bristol from 1800 until his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Layard was educated at St John's College, Cambridge. He was ordained deacon on 21 December 1771; and priest on 27 February 1774. He was the Minister at the Oxenden Chapel, a daughter church of St Martin-in-the-Fields before holdin
2 CONC g incumbencies in Wootton Bassett, Uffington and Kewstoke.
2 CONT
2 CONT Layard's daughter Charlotte Susanna Elizabeth married, as his second wife, Albemarle Bertie, 9th Earl of Lindsey and was mother of Lady Charlotte Guest. Other children were:
2 CONT
2 CONT The eldest son, Brownlow Villiers Layard, an army officer who became a cleric. Henry Peter John Layard of the Ceylon civil service, father of Austen Henry Layard
2 CONT
2 CONT * Birth: 19 February 1748/49 at London, England. 
2 CONT * Parents: Daniel Peter Layard and Susanne Henriette de Boisragon. 
2 CONT * Wife 1: Elizabeth Ann Carver Ward, daughter of Joseph Ward and Ruth Carver, on 1 December 1777 at Greenwich, Kent, England. 
2 CONT * Wife 2: Elizabeth Carver on 24 October 1798. 
2 CONT * Death: 11 April 1803 at age 54.
2 CONT
2 CONT * He was educated at Huntingdon School.
2 CONT * He graduated from St. John's College, Oxford University, Oxford, Oxfordshire, England, in 1770 with a Bachelor of Arts (B.A.).
2 CONT * He graduated from St. John's College, Oxford University, Oxford, Oxfordshire, England, in 1773 with a Master of Arts (M.A.).
2 CONT * He was the Vicar at St. Martin in the Field, Westminster, London, England.
2 CONT * He was the Vicar between 1777 and 1799 at Kewstock, Somerset, England.
2 CONT * He was invested as a Fellow, Royal Society (F.R.S.) in 1778.
2 CONT * He graduated from St. John's College, Oxford University, Oxford, Oxfordshire, England, in 1787 with a Doctor of Divinity (D.D.).
2 CONT * He held the office of Prebendary of Worcester in 1793.3 He was the Rector between 1798 and 1803 at Uffington, Leicestershire, England.
2 CONT * He held the office of Prebendary of Bangor between 1799 and 1803.
2 CONT * He held the office of Dean of Bristol between 1800 and 1803.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Very Rev. Charles Peter Layard and Elizabeth Ann Carver Ward
2 CONT * Reverend Brownlow Villiers Layard b. 19 Jan 1779, d. 26 Mar 1861
2 CONT * Charlotte Susannah Elizabeth Layard b. 21 Mar 1780, d. 28 Nov 1858
2 CONT * Marianne Layard b. 21 Mar 1781, d. 1840
2 CONT * Henrietta Margaret Layard b. 21 Mar 1782, d. 14 Aug 1855
2 CONT * Henry Peter John Layard b. 15 Jul 1783, d. 4 Oct 1834
2 CONT * Sophia Catherine Layard b. 2 Aug 1784, d. 24 Mar 1785
2 CONT * Charles Edward Layard b. 18 Oct 1786, d. 5 May 1852
2 CONT * Caroline Bethia Layard b. 24 Oct 1787, d. 4 Jan 1827
2 CONT * Caroline Layard b. 27 Mar 1788, d. 4 Jan 1827
2 CONT * Louisa Frances Layard b. 19 Jun 1789, d. 3 Mar 1851
2 CONT * Mary Sarah Sophia Layard b. 28 Oct 1791, d. 1868
2 CONT * Elizabeth Frances Layard b. 2 Jun 1793, d. 16 Feb 1857
2 CONT * Jane Isabella Layard b. 8 Sep 1795, d. 22 Jul 1796
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations:
2 CONT * Bourkes Peerage 2003 volume 2, page 2349
2 CONT *[http://www.thepeerage.com/p2615.htm#i26143 The Peerage]
