1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===SIR DAVID MURRAY OF STANHOPE Baronet===
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Sir David Murray, Baronet [S. 1664], of Stanhope and Broughton</strong>, 1st s. and h. ; M.P. [S.] for Peeblesshire, 1681-82 and 1689, till declared void, in 1693, for not having taken the oaths. He appears to have favour
2 CONC ed the Rising of 1715. In 1726 he purchased the estate of Ardnamurchan and the lead mines of Strontian. He m. firstly, 16 April 1684, Anne, da. of Alexander (Bruce), 2d Earl of Kincardine [S.], by Veronica, da. of Corneille Van So
2 CONC mmelsdyck. He m. secondly in or before 1714, Margaret, widow of Thomas Scott, of Whitslaid, da. of Sir John Scott, 1st Baronet [1671], of Ancrum, by his 2d wife, Elizabeth, da. of Sir William Bennet, of 
2 CONT Grubbet. He d. 14 and was bur. 17 Feb. 1729, in the Canongate churchyard, Edinburgh. His widow d. 5 Sep. 1761."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/cu31924092524390#page/n361/mode/2up Complete baronetage]; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1903; Vol. III; page 342
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
