2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''5 March 1714: Conjoined Processes of Separation, Aliment, etc.: Grizell Baillie and others v Alexander Murray. Grizell Baillie, spouse to Alexander Murray, younger of Stanhope, eldest son and heir to Sir David Murray of Stanhop
2 CONC e, advocate, and George Baillie of Jerviswood her father, and Lady Grizell Baillie, her mother, for their interests, against the said Alexander Murray - et e contra, marriage contract dated 16 August 1710. [http://catalogue.nrscot
2 CONC land.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=CC8%2f6%2f167&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=david+murray+of+stanhope&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1707&dt=1755&di=n National Records of Scotland, Edinburgh Commissary Court, reference CC8/6/16
2 CONC 7]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''4 August 1724-1735: Bond of relief by William Home of Linthill, to Sir Robert Dalrymple of Castletoun, of bond by said Sir Robert, Mr. John Swinton of that ilk, advocate, and himself to Sir David Murray of Stanhope, for 1000 me
2 CONC rks scots; with related papers. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD110%2f504&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=david+murray+of+stanhope&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1707&dt=1755&di=n National Records of Sc
2 CONC otland, Papers of the Hamilton-Dalrymple Family of North Berwick, reference GD110/504]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''29 July 1734: Petition to lords of council and session by Charles Murray, son of Sir David Murray of Stanhope, on behalf of himself and of the Duke of Norfolk, praying that he may be granted possession of mines in baronies of S
2 CONC tanhope and Stobo, sheriffdom of Peebles, and Ardnamurchan, sheriffdom of Argyle [Argyll], which had been leased to Governor and Company of Undertakers for raising Thames Water in York Buildings, but which said Company had failed 
2 CONC to work; and relevant productions. (Printed). [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD124%2f6%2f230&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=david+murray+of+stanhope&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1707&dt=1755&di=n Nati
2 CONC onal Records of Scotland, Papers of the Erskine Family, Earls of Mar and Kellie, reference GD124/6/230]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''11 May 1748: Process of Declarator of Marriage etc.: Mrs Ann Murray v William Henry Cranstoun. Mrs Ann Murray, eldest lawful daughter to the deceased David Murray merchant in Leith, lawful son to the deceased Sir David Murray o
2 CONC f Stanhope, spouse to Lieutenant William Henry Cranstoun of the Regiment of Marines, commanded lately by Colonel Jeffries, now by Sir Andrew Agnew, and Jean Cranstoun, their daughter, against the said William Henry Cranstoun, marr
2 CONC ied May 1744, and had issue Jean, born 19 February 1745. Several papers badly damaged by damp. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=CC8%2f6%2f323&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=david+murray+of+
