2 CONT "<strong>Sir Alexander Murray, Baronet [S. 1664], of Stanhope and Broughton</strong>, 2d but 1st surv. s. and h. ; was M.P. for Peeblesshire, 1710-12 and in 1734; suc. to the Baronetcy , 14 Feb.1729; sold the estate of Broughton, 
2 CONC about 1738, to his younger br., John Murray. He m. (contract, 16 June 1710) Grizel, da. of George Baillie, of Jerviswood, co. Lanark, and of Mellerstaine, co. Berwick (one of the Lords of the Treasury), by Grizel, da. of Patrick (
2 CONC Home), 1st Earl of Marchmont [S.]. He d. s.p. 18 May 1743, when part of his estate remained in the hands of his creditors. His widow d. 6 June 1759, in her 68th year."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/cu31924092524390#page/n361/mode/2up Complete baronetage]; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1903; Vol. III; page 342-343
