1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Sir Charles Murray, Baronet [S. 1644]</strong>, a Collector of Customs at Bo'ness, co. Linlithgow, uncle of the whole blood and h. male, being 5th s. of the 2d Baronet by his first wife, suc. to the Baronetcy on the death
2 CONC  of his nephew, but it is doubtful whether he ever assumed the title. He m. firstly, in 1733, "a lady with £16,000." He m. secondly Isabella, widow of Hugh Dalrymple Murray, of Melgund and Kynynmond, da. and coheir of Hugh Somervi
2 CONC lle, of Inverteil, co. Fife. She d. 8 Dec. 1760. He d. 1770."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/cu31924092524390#page/n361/mode/2up Complete baronetage]; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1903; Vol. III; page 343
2 CONT
2 CONT "(321) <strong>(Sir) Charles Murray (fifth Baronet)</strong>, fifth son of Sir David (No. 318), died 1770. Will recorded 13th December 1770 (Edinburgh). His second wife was Isabella, daughter of Hugh Somerville of Inverteil, by wh
2 CONC om he had a son"
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://www.archive.org/stream/heraldryofmurray00john#page/76/mode/2up The heraldry of the Murrays: with notes on all the males of the family, descriptions of the arms, plates and pedigrees], by G. Harvey Johnston, 1910, 
2 CONC page 76, paragraph 321
2 CONT --------------------
