1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.thepeerage.com/p12955.htm#i129542
2 CONT
2 CONT Nanfan Coote, 2nd Earl of Bellomont was born circa 1681.1 He was the son of Richard Coote, 1st Earl of Bellomont and Catherine Nanfan.1 He married Lucia Anna de Nassau, Countess de Nassau, daughter of Henry de Nassau, Count of Nas
2 CONC sau and Frances van Aersen, on 17 February 1705/6 at St. Martin-in-the-Fields Church, Covent Garden, London, England.1 He died on 14 June 1708 at Bath, Somerset, England, from palsy, without male issue.1 He was buried on 16 June 1
2 CONC 708 at Bath Abbey, Bath, Somerset, England.1 He died intestate and his estate was administered on 23 August 1709.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Nanfan Coote, 2nd Earl of Bellomont succeeded to the title of 3rd Lord Coote, Baron of Coloony, co. Sligo [I., 1660] on 5 March 1700/1.2 He succeeded to the title of 2nd Earl of Bellomont, in our Kingdom of Ireland [I., 1689] on 5
2 CONC  March 1700/1.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Nanfan Coote, 2nd Earl of Bellomont and Lucia Anna de Nassau, Countess de Nassau
2 CONT * Lady Frances Coote+1 d. 1733
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Citations''
2 CONT * [S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Extinc
2 CONC t or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume II, page 108. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT * [S6] Cokayne, and others, The Complete Peerage, volume III, page 416.
