1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Jeanne-Pernette Schenker-Massot=
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jeanne-Pernette_Schenker-Massot '''Jeanne-Pernette Schenker-Massot'''], often referred to simply as '''Pernette Massot''' was a Swiss miniaturist, pastellist, and engraver.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Born in Geneva''', Schenker-Massot was the elder sister of the painter [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Firmin_Massot '''Firmin Massot'''], and has traditionally been described as his first teacher.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Her own teacher''' is said to have been '''Jean-Baptiste Carvelle''', a French expatriate in Switzerland.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In 1794 she married''' the miniaturist and engraver '''Nicolas Schenker''', with whom she had two children.
