1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/De_Geer_af_Leufsta_nr_131#TAB_11 '''''Louis'' Carl Gerard Etienne De Geer af Leufsta'''], head after his father 1947-04-04. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Born 1887-12-22''' in Eaux-Vives. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Graduated with a law''' degree from Uppsala University in 1916. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Served in Östersysslets''' domsaga 1916-1918. Diplomatic trainee (attaché) in the Ministry of Foreign Affairs 1918. Acting 2nd legation secretary in the Ministry of Foreign Affairs 1919. Acting 2nd legation secretary at the mis
2 CONC sion in Rome 1920. RNedONO 1920. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Acting legation secretary''' 1921 and in Bern 1922. RFrHL 1922. First legation secretary in the Ministry of Foreign Affairs  1923. Secretary to the Minister for Foreign Affairs 1923. KItKrO 1923. GVPostJubM 1924. KAbessSO 1924.
2 CONC  KTunNIO 1925. RFinlVRO1kl 1925. ÖRKOffHtm with war decorations. Resignation and 1st legation secretary in dispensation 1928. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Chamberlain 1928'''. Introducer for foreign envoys 1928. RNO 1929. Legation Council in dispensability 1930. StOffLettSO. KNO2kl 1934. KNO1kl 1938. Title of ministre plénipotentiaire 1940. StOffAbessMenO. StOffBKrO. StOffRumSO. 
2 CONC KFrHl. JUSO3kl. sm. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Held the fideikommisse''' estates [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/L%C3%B6vstabruk Leufsta] and Hamarby-Väsby, both in Uppland, the house no. 6 at Kungsängsgatan in Uppsala and fideikommisskapital. 1950. GV:sMt 1951. KmstkNO 1952
2 CONC . 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Died 1953-04-20''' Lövsta parish, Uppsala county. ''Biography'' in ''Who's Who''? 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Married 1916-09-09''' in Eaux-Vives to [https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Tersmeden_nr_1940#TAB_7 '''Augusta Christina Elisabeth (''Beth'') Tersmeden'''], born 1890-09-28 at Hinseberg in Näsby parish, Örebro county, KNedOHO1
2 CONC kl 1957-05-00. GMsjv 1961-10-20, died 1968-07-21. Daughter of mill owner Conrad Jakob August Tersmeden and Julie Hammarhjelm-Strokirk.
