1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Auguste Reverdin=
2 CONT
2 CONT Auguste Reverdin (born in Geneva the December 2, 1848, died in the same city on June 18, 1908) was a Swiss doctor, surgeon and teacher. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography===  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Younger son''' of '''Jaques Pierre Jean Reverdin''', banker in Geneva, and '''Amélie Augustine Janot''', Auguste Reverdin studied medicine at the University of Strasbourg, where he obtained a doctorate in 1874, and also at Pari
2 CONC s. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''After his studies''', he worked for the Paris ambulance service and also worked in foreign hospitals. In 1879, Auguste Reverdin returned to Geneva, where he founded the first private clinic in the city the same year with the ar
2 CONC chitect Adolphe Reverdin (his grandfather) and [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jaques-Louis_Reverdin '''Jaques Louis Reverdin'''] (his first cousin). 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Auguste Reverdin''' performed many thyroidectomies and carefully documented his observations which he published in 1883. In 1887 Reverdin was appointed private tutor, then professor of surgery at the'University of Geneva in 189
2 CONC 9.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Auguste Reverdin''' is the inventor of several medical instruments, as well as anesthesia and disinfection equipment. In 1895 he won an important medical prize in the'National Academy of Medicine in Paris, the price Labor, join
2 CONC tly with Professor Léon Massol, thanks to his work Antisepsis and Surgical Asepsis. He was also honored with several foreign awards and was a member of several medical organizations, including the Society of cremating corpses, the
2 CONC  National Academy of Medicine (since May 28, 1901) and the Paris Surgery Society. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In september 1898''', he performed an autopsy of the empress's body [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Empress_Elisabeth_of_Austria '''Elisabeth of Austria'''] (known as «'''Sissi'''» ), murdered in Geneva.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In 1904 Auguste Reverdin''' was one of the many doctors who appointed [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C3%89lie_Metchnikoff '''Ilya Ilych Metchnikov'''] for the Nobel Prize in medicine, which was finally won by [https://fr.wikip
2 CONC edia.org/wiki/Ivan_Pavlov '''Ivan Petrovich Pavlov''']. Metsjnikov later won this Nobel Prize in 1908. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Auguste Reverdin''', husband of '''Thérèse Agnès Patron''' since 1880  is the father of'[https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Albert_Reverdin '''Albert Reverdin'''], who is a doctor, too.
2 CONT
2 CONT * https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Auguste_Reverdin
