1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Albert Reverdin=
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Albert Reverdin''' was a surgeon in Geneva. He was the son of [https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Auguste_Reverdin '''Auguste Reverdin'''] and the nephew of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jaques-Louis_Reverdin '''Jaques-Louis Reverd
2 CONC in'''].
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He studied medicine''' under [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/C%C3%A9sar_Roux '''Caesar Roux'''] at the hospital of Lausanne.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He served as a doctor''' for the Vaud-Geneva ambulance set up by the Red Cross during the Greco-Turkish War (1912-1913), a period in which he became close to Princess [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marie_Bonaparte '''Marie Bona
2 CONC parte''']. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''During the First''' World War, he was head of surgery at the Bourg-en-Bresse military hospital, where he worked alongside [https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marie_Long-Landry '''Marie Long-Landry'''].
2 CONT
2 CONT * https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Albert_Reverdin
